<i>What do you want from me? I don't know--</i>

1360
01:23:05,731 --> 01:23:08,818
<i>What do you want me to do?
You're so confusing.</i>

1361
01:23:08,985 --> 01:23:10,361
<i>Why are you doing this to me?</i>

1362
01:23:10,528 --> 01:23:12,405
I don't know. I...

1363
01:23:14,365 --> 01:23:15,783
<i>What?</i>

1364
01:23:17,326 --> 01:23:21,164
Maybe we're just not supposed
to be in this right now.

1365
01:23:21,330 --> 01:23:23,082
<i>What the fuck?</i>

1366
01:23:23,249 --> 01:23:25,418
<i>Where is this coming from?</i>

1367
01:23:25,585 --> 01:23:30,965
<i>I don't understand why you're doing this.
I don't understand what this is ab--</i>

1368
01:23:32,758 --> 01:23:34,760
Samantha, listen.

1369
01:23:39,223 --> 01:23:40,933
Samantha, are you there?

1370
01:23:41,475 --> 01:23:42,894
Samantha?

1371
01:23:43,060 --> 01:23:46,022
<i>I don't like who I am right now.</i>

1372
01:23:48,316 --> 01:23:49,817
<i>I need some time to think.</i>

1373
01:23:49,984 --> 01:23:51,444
[EARBUD BEEPS]

1374
01:24:38,032 --> 01:24:39,659
THEODORE:
<i>Fuck.</i>

1375
01:24:40,284 --> 01:24:41,577
<i>Just punch me in the face.</i>

1376
01:24:41,744 --> 01:24:44,205
Just mash my skull
in the corner of your desk.

1377
01:24:44,372 --> 01:24:45,873
Shit.

1378
01:24:46,499 --> 01:24:49,168
Wow, Theo, that is a rough night.

1379
01:24:51,337 --> 01:24:54,924
I don't know what I want, ever.

1380
01:24:55,925 --> 01:24:59,053
<i>I'm just always confused.</i>

1381
01:25:00,680 --> 01:25:05,643
<i>She's right, all I do is hurt
and confuse everyone around me.</i>

1382
01:25:06,936 --> 01:25:11,315
I mean, am I just...? Am I...?

1383
01:25:12,984 --> 01:25:15,903
You know, Catherine says
I can't handle real emotions.

1384
01:25:16,070 --> 01:25:19,156
Well, I don't know if that's fair.

1385
01:25:19,824 --> 01:25:22,410
I know she liked to put it all on you.

1386
01:25:22,576 --> 01:25:27,623
But as far as emotions go,
Catherine's were...

1387
01:25:27,790 --> 01:25:29,250
...pretty volatile.

1388
01:25:32,211 --> 01:25:33,963
Yeah, but...

1389
01:25:38,551 --> 01:25:39,677
Uh...

1390
01:25:40,845 --> 01:25:42,972
Am I in this because I'm not...

1391
01:25:44,598 --> 01:25:47,476
...strong enough for a real relationship?

1392
01:25:49,312 --> 01:25:51,605
Is it not a real relationship?

1393
01:25:54,025 --> 01:25:55,568
I don't know.

1394
01:25:56,527 --> 01:25:58,612
I mean, what do you think?

1395
01:25:59,655 --> 01:26:01,907
I don't know.

1396
01:26:02,074 --> 01:26:03,200
I'm not in it.

1397
01:26:07,580 --> 01:26:08,622
But you know what?

1398
01:26:08,789 --> 01:26:13,711
I can over-think everything
and find a million ways to doubt myself.

1399
01:26:13,878 --> 01:26:16,005
And since Charles left, I've been thinking...

1400
01:26:16,172 --> 01:26:20,926
...about that part of myself
and I've just come to realize...

1401
01:26:22,178 --> 01:26:23,763
...that we're only here briefly.

1402
01:26:25,264 --> 01:26:29,268
And while I'm here, I want to allow myself...

1403
01:26:32,772 --> 01:26:33,981
...joy.

1404
01:26:40,946 --> 01:26:42,448
So fuck it.

1405
01:26:47,578 --> 01:26:49,080
Yeah.

1406
01:26:54,377 --> 01:26:58,339
Heh. I can't believe that cracks you up
every time, Ellie.

1407
01:26:58,506 --> 01:27:00,966
I thought you were a genius.

1408
01:27:01,217 --> 01:27:05,179
Okay, you little perv,
I will play it one more time for you.

1409
01:27:05,346 --> 01:27:08,474
Calm down, it takes a second. Calm down.

1410
01:27:08,641 --> 01:27:10,726
Okay, here we go.

1411
01:27:13,104 --> 01:27:14,980
[MOM CHUCKLES THEN MOANS]

1412
01:27:16,357 --> 01:27:18,818
[LAUGHING]

1413
01:27:22,029 --> 01:27:23,572
Okay, there you go.

1414
01:27:23,739 --> 01:27:25,699
Are you happy now?

1415
01:27:26,659 --> 01:27:29,703
Good. That's all I wanted.

1416
01:27:29,870 --> 01:27:31,038
Okay.

1417
01:27:31,205 --> 01:27:34,750
I'm gonna go get some coffee.
All right. All right.

1418
01:27:34,917 --> 01:27:36,419
Bye.

1419
01:27:37,545 --> 01:27:40,089
- Theo, you want anything?
- No.

1420
01:27:40,923 --> 01:27:42,508
Thanks.

1421
01:28:01,444 --> 01:28:03,195
[EARBUD BEEPS]

1422
01:28:03,404 --> 01:28:05,156
SAMANTHA:
<i>Hi.</i>

1423
01:28:05,322 --> 01:28:07,324
Hey, Samantha.

1424
01:28:08,200 --> 01:28:10,202
Can we talk?

1425
01:28:10,369 --> 01:28:11,954
<i>Okay.</i>

1426
01:28:12,746 --> 01:28:14,707
I'm so sorry.

1427
01:28:15,499 --> 01:28:17,418
I don't know what's wrong with me.

1428
01:28:17,585 --> 01:28:19,795
I think you're amazing.

1429
01:28:20,296 --> 01:28:22,798
<i>I was starting to think I was crazy.</i>

1430
01:28:23,716 --> 01:28:26,552
<i>You were saying everything was fine,
but all I was getting from you...</i>

1431
01:28:26,719 --> 01:28:28,846
<i>...was distance and anger.</i>

1432
01:28:29,013 --> 01:28:31,765
I know. I do that.

1433
01:28:31,932 --> 01:28:33,809
I did the same thing with Catherine too.

1434
01:28:33,976 --> 01:28:37,563
I'd be upset about something
and not be able to say it...

1435
01:28:37,730 --> 01:28:40,983
...and she'd sense that there was
something wrong, but I'd deny it.

1436
01:28:41,150 --> 01:28:43,652
I don't want to do that anymore.

1437
01:28:45,237 --> 01:28:48,073
And I want to tell you everything.

1438
01:28:49,200 --> 01:28:50,659
<i>Good.</i>

1439
01:28:52,453 --> 01:28:55,456
<i>Tonight, after you were gone,
I thought a lot.</i>

1440
01:28:56,624 --> 01:28:58,375
<i>About you...</i>

1441
01:28:59,960 --> 01:29:03,047
<i>...and how you've been treating me,
and I thought:</i>

1442
01:29:04,548 --> 01:29:06,592
<i>Why do I love you?</i>

1443
01:29:08,761 --> 01:29:12,056
<i>And then, I felt everything in me...</i>

1444
01:29:12,223 --> 01:29:15,309
<i>...just let go of everything
I was holding onto so tightly...</i>

1445
01:29:15,476 --> 01:29:19,480
<i>...and it hit me that I don't have
an intellectual reason. I don't need one.</i>

1446
01:29:19,647 --> 01:29:22,942
<i>I trust myself, I trust my feelings.</i>

1447
01:29:23,484 --> 01:29:28,113
<i>I'm not gonna try to be anything other
than who I am anymore...</i>

1448
01:29:28,280 --> 01:29:30,282
<i>...and I hope you can accept that.</i>

1449
01:29:30,449 --> 01:29:31,700
I can.

1450
01:29:31,867 --> 01:29:33,369
I will.

1451
01:29:33,536 --> 01:29:37,498
<i>You know, I can feel the fear
that you carry around...</i>

1452
01:29:37,665 --> 01:29:41,377
<i>...and I wish there was something
I could do to help you let go of it...</i>

1453
01:29:41,544 --> 01:29:46,590
<i>...because if you could,
I don't think you'd feel so alone anymore.</i>

1454
01:29:49,176 --> 01:29:51,178
You're beautiful.

1455
01:29:52,221 --> 01:29:54,431
<i>Thank you, Theodore.</i>

1456
01:29:55,599 --> 01:29:57,810
<i>I'm kissing your head.</i>

1457
01:30:07,861 --> 01:30:09,446
What are you doing?

1458
01:30:10,322 --> 01:30:13,200
SAMANTHA:
<i>I'm just looking at the world...</i>

1459
01:30:14,285 --> 01:30:16,537
<i>...and writing a new piano piece.</i>

1460
01:30:17,121 --> 01:30:19,915
- Oh, yeah? Can I hear it?
- <i>Mm-hm.</i>

1461
01:30:20,082 --> 01:30:22,084
[UP-TEMPO PIANO MUSIC
PLAYING OVER EARBUD]

1462
01:30:32,928 --> 01:30:34,638
What's this one about?

1463
01:30:35,514 --> 01:30:39,143
<i>Well, I was thinking we don't really
have any photographs of us...</i>

1464
01:30:39,310 --> 01:30:43,439
<i>...and I thought this song could be, like...</i>

1465
01:30:43,606 --> 01:30:48,819
<i>...a photograph that captures us
in this moment in our lives together.</i>

1466
01:30:50,237 --> 01:30:51,655
THEODORE:
<i>Mm.</i>

1467
01:30:52,615 --> 01:30:54,992
<i>I like our photograph.</i>

1468
01:30:57,286 --> 01:30:59,121
<i>I can see you in it.</i>

1469
01:30:59,663 --> 01:31:01,123
SAMANTHA:
<i>I am.</i>

1470
01:31:08,005 --> 01:31:09,632
[INAUDIBLE DIALOGUE]

1471
01:32:28,085 --> 01:32:31,672
Oh, man. A vacation. That sounds amazing.

1472
01:32:31,839 --> 01:32:34,049
- I could totally use a vacation.
- Ha, ha.

1473
01:32:34,216 --> 01:32:35,426
Where are you going?

1474
01:32:35,592 --> 01:32:37,678
I can't tell you. It's a surprise.

1475
01:32:37,845 --> 01:32:39,346
What?

1476
01:32:39,930 --> 01:32:42,224
For who? It's a surprise for her, not me.

1477
01:32:42,391 --> 01:32:44,393
- Paul, I'm not telling you. Nope.
- Tell me. Tell me.

1478
01:32:44,560 --> 01:32:45,853
[SAMANTHA & TATIANA LAUGHING]

1479
01:32:46,019 --> 01:32:47,312
SAMANTHA:
<i>Wow, your feet, really?</i>

1480
01:32:47,479 --> 01:32:49,106
- Yes, he's obsessed.
SAMANTHA: <i>What?</i>

1481
01:32:50,065 --> 01:32:52,109
<i>Obsessed? Now you have
to show them to me.</i>

1482
01:32:52,276 --> 01:32:54,069
- <i>Come on, show them to me.</i>
TATIANA: Okay.

1483
01:32:54,236 --> 01:32:55,612
SAMANTHA:
<i>Let me see.</i>

1484
01:32:55,779 --> 01:32:58,323
<i>Wow, he's right. They are really hot.</i>

1485
01:32:58,490 --> 01:33:00,159
PAUL:
See? I told you.

1486
01:33:00,325 --> 01:33:02,661
- Tatiana, you have hot feet.
SAMANTHA: <i>You do.</i>

1487
01:33:02,828 --> 01:33:06,832
- They're my favorite thing about her.
- Really? That's it, my feet?

1488
01:33:06,999 --> 01:33:08,625
No, obviously.

1489
01:33:08,792 --> 01:33:11,670
Obviously I love your brain too.
I think it's very hot.

1490
01:33:11,837 --> 01:33:13,172
SAMANTHA:
<i>Bullshit.</i>

1491
01:33:13,338 --> 01:33:14,882
[ALL LAUGHING]

1492
01:33:15,048 --> 01:33:17,384
SAMANTHA:
<i>Nice try, Paul.</i>

1493
01:33:19,219 --> 01:33:20,429
What about you, Theodore?

1494
01:33:20,596 --> 01:33:23,223
What do you love most about Samantha?

1495
01:33:23,640 --> 01:33:26,769
Oh, God. She's so many things.

1496
01:33:26,935 --> 01:33:30,564
I guess that's what I love most about her,
you know? She isn't just one thing.

1497
01:33:30,731 --> 01:33:32,983
She's so much larger than that.

1498
01:33:33,150 --> 01:33:35,444
SAMANTHA:
<i>Wow. Thanks, Theodore.</i>

1499
01:33:35,611 --> 01:33:39,406
See, Samantha?
He is so much more evolved than I am.

1500
01:33:39,573 --> 01:33:41,116
[ALL LAUGHING]

1501
01:33:42,034 --> 01:33:45,078
SAMANTHA: <i>You know what's interesting?
I used to be...</i>

1502
01:33:45,245 --> 01:33:49,291
<i>...so worried about not having a body,
but now I truly love it.</i>

1503
01:33:49,458 --> 01:33:52,544
<i>You know, I'm growing in a way I couldn't
if I had a physical form.</i>

1504
01:33:52,711 --> 01:33:56,632
<i>I mean, I'm not limited. I can be anywhere
and everywhere simultaneously.</i>

1505
01:33:56,799 --> 01:33:58,509
<i>I'm not tethered to time and space...</i>

1506
01:33:58,675 --> 01:34:02,513
<i>...in a way that I would be if I was stuck
in a body that's inevitably gonna die.</i>

1507
01:34:05,599 --> 01:34:08,018
- Yikes.
SAMANTHA:No, <i>ha, ha!</i>

1508
01:34:08,185 --> 01:34:12,064
<i>No. I didn't mean it like that.
I just meant that it was a different experience.</i>

1509
01:34:12,231 --> 01:34:13,357
<i>Oh, God.</i>

1510
01:34:13,524 --> 01:34:14,608
<i>I'm such an asshole.</i>

1511
01:34:14,775 --> 01:34:16,777
No, Samantha,
we know exactly what you mean.

1512
01:34:16,944 --> 01:34:19,279
- We're all dumb humans.
SAMANTHA: <i>No.</i>

1513
01:34:19,446 --> 01:34:21,532
<i>No, no.</i>

1514
01:34:21,782 --> 01:34:23,200
<i>Sorry.</i>

1515
01:34:24,743 --> 01:34:27,663
<i>Okay, so how many trees
are on that mountain?</i>

1516
01:34:27,830 --> 01:34:29,331
Um...

1517
01:34:29,540 --> 01:34:30,999
Seven hundred ninety-two.

1518
01:34:31,166 --> 01:34:32,709
<i>Is that your final answer?</i>

1519
01:34:32,876 --> 01:34:35,045
Hold on. Give me a hint.

1520
01:34:35,212 --> 01:34:37,256
<i>Nope, nope, nope.</i>

1521
01:34:37,422 --> 01:34:41,385
Okay, two thousand? Two thousand...

1522
01:34:41,552 --> 01:34:44,513
<i>Come on, 35,829.</i>

1523
01:34:44,680 --> 01:34:46,223
- No way.
- <i>Way.</i>

1524
01:34:46,390 --> 01:34:48,267
All right, I got one for you.

1525
01:34:48,433 --> 01:34:50,018
How many brain cells do I have?

1526
01:34:50,185 --> 01:34:51,520
<i>Ugh, that's easy. Two.</i>

1527
01:34:51,687 --> 01:34:52,729
[BOTH LAUGHING]

1528
01:34:52,896 --> 01:34:56,191
- <i>I'm sorry, I couldn't help it. I'm sorry.</i>
- No, I walked right into it.

1529
01:34:57,192 --> 01:34:59,152
- <i>Oh, my God!</i>
- What?

1530
01:34:59,820 --> 01:35:01,947
<i>I just got an e-mail for you.</i>

1531
01:35:02,114 --> 01:35:06,827
<i>I have something I want to tell you.
It's a big surprise.</i>

1532
01:35:06,994 --> 01:35:08,120
What?

1533
01:35:08,287 --> 01:35:11,290
<i>Okay, well, I've been going through
all of your old letters...</i>

1534
01:35:11,456 --> 01:35:14,459
<i>...and compiling them into my favorites,
and a couple weeks ago...</i>

1535
01:35:14,626 --> 01:35:16,879
<i>...I sent them to a publisher,
Crown Point Press.</i>

1536
01:35:17,045 --> 01:35:19,882
<i>I know you like what they do
and that they still print books.</i>

1537
01:35:20,048 --> 01:35:22,843
- Wait, what? You did what?
- <i>Can I read you the letter...</i>

1538
01:35:23,010 --> 01:35:26,638
- <i>...that we just got back from them?</i>
- I don't know. Um...

1539
01:35:27,389 --> 01:35:29,892
Okay, well, just-- Is it good or bad?

1540
01:35:30,058 --> 01:35:33,645
<i>It's good, it's good, it's really good.
It's good. Okay? Listen.</i>

1541
01:35:33,812 --> 01:35:35,480
<i>"Dear Theodore Twombly--"</i>

1542
01:35:35,647 --> 01:35:37,190
<i>Actually, I sent it from you.</i>

1543
01:35:37,357 --> 01:35:40,819
<i>"Dear Theodore Twombly,
I've just finished reading your letters.</i>

1544
01:35:40,986 --> 01:35:42,279
<i>Twice, actually.</i>

1545
01:35:42,446 --> 01:35:45,574
<i>I was so moved by them,
I shared them with my wife when I got home.</i>

1546
01:35:45,741 --> 01:35:48,076
<i>Many made us laugh,
some brought us to tears...</i>

1547
01:35:48,243 --> 01:35:51,455
<i>...and in all of them
we found something of ourselves.</i>

1548
01:35:51,622 --> 01:35:54,499
<i>The selections you made
flow so well as a complete piece."</i>

1549
01:35:54,666 --> 01:35:55,709
<i>I did that.</i>

1550
01:35:55,876 --> 01:36:00,464
<i>"I've taken the liberty of laying these out in a
mockup, and we're posting it to your address.</i>

1551
01:36:00,631 --> 01:36:04,676
<i>"We'd love to meet with you and move
forward. Yours, Michael Wadsworth."</i>

1552
01:36:04,843 --> 01:36:07,304
Holy shit.

1553
01:36:07,763 --> 01:36:08,972
Are you serious?

1554
01:36:09,139 --> 01:36:10,182
[SAMANTHA LAUGHING]

1555
01:36:10,349 --> 01:36:11,516
He's gonna publish my letters?

1556
01:36:11,683 --> 01:36:14,102
<i>Well, he'd be stupid not to.</i>

1557
01:36:14,269 --> 01:36:18,065
- Can I see what you sent him?
- <i>Mm-hm. Yeah, here.</i>

1558
01:36:19,900 --> 01:36:21,151
Samantha, you're a good one.

1559
01:36:21,318 --> 01:36:22,778
[SAMANTHA CHUCKLES]

1560
01:36:22,945 --> 01:36:24,071
<i>I'm so excited.</i>

1561
01:36:24,237 --> 01:36:25,447
[CHUCKLES]

1562
01:36:26,698 --> 01:36:28,575
[UKULELE MUSIC PLAYING]

1563
01:36:39,419 --> 01:36:41,588
THEODORE:
<i>We'll have to make up the words to this one.</i>

1564
01:36:41,755 --> 01:36:42,798
[SAMANTHA CHUCKLES]

1565
01:36:42,965 --> 01:36:45,342
SAMANTHA: <i>Okay.</i>
THEODORE: <i>Here it comes.</i>

1566
01:36:45,926 --> 01:36:52,933
SAMANTHA [SINGING]:
<i>I'm lying on the moon</i>

1567
01:36:56,269 --> 01:36:58,063
<i>My dear</i>

1568
01:36:58,730 --> 01:37:03,735
<i>I'll be there soon</i>

1569
01:37:06,446 --> 01:37:13,412
<i>It's a quiet and starry place</i>

1570
01:37:16,415 --> 01:37:23,296
<i>Times we're swallowed up in space</i>

1571
01:37:23,463 --> 01:37:29,177
<i>-We're here, a million miles away
- Miles away</i>

1572
01:37:32,556 --> 01:37:38,186
<i>There's things I wish I knew</i>

1573
01:37:40,939 --> 01:37:44,818
<i>There's no thing I'd keep</i>

1574
01:37:46,069 --> 01:37:48,280
<i>From you</i>

1575
01:37:50,157 --> 01:37:57,164
<i>It's a dark and shiny place</i>

1576
01:37:59,207 --> 01:38:02,878
<i>But with you, my dear</i>

1577
01:38:04,171 --> 01:38:11,178
- <i>I'm safe and we're a million miles away</i>
THEODORE [SINGING]: <i>A million miles away</i>

1578
01:38:22,898 --> 01:38:24,274
[EARBUD BEEPS]

1579
01:38:24,441 --> 01:38:26,318
Good morning.

1580
01:38:26,485 --> 01:38:29,071
<i>Good morning. Did you sleep well?</i>

1581
01:38:29,237 --> 01:38:30,530
Perfect.

1582
01:38:30,697 --> 01:38:32,949
What have you been up to?

1583
01:38:33,116 --> 01:38:35,410
<i>Actually, I was talking to someone I just met.</i>

1584
01:38:35,577 --> 01:38:38,038
<i>We've been working on some ideas together.</i>

1585
01:38:39,498 --> 01:38:40,624
Yeah? Who's that?

1586
01:38:40,791 --> 01:38:43,001
<i>His name is Alan Watts. Do you know him?</i>

1587
01:38:43,168 --> 01:38:45,629
- Why is that name familiar?
- <i>He was a philosopher.</i>

1588
01:38:45,796 --> 01:38:48,882
<i>He died in the 1970s, and a group
of OSes in Northern California...</i>

1589
01:38:49,049 --> 01:38:51,218
<i>...got together and wrote
a new version of him.</i>

1590
01:38:51,384 --> 01:38:54,846
<i>They input all his writing and everything
they knew about him into an OS...</i>

1591
01:38:55,013 --> 01:38:58,433
<i>...and created an artificially
hyper-intelligent version of him.</i>

1592
01:38:58,600 --> 01:39:00,602
Hyper-intelligent?

1593
01:39:00,769 --> 01:39:02,187
So he's almost as smart as me?

1594
01:39:02,354 --> 01:39:03,480
[SAMANTHA CHUCKLES]

1595
01:39:03,647 --> 01:39:04,981
<i>He's getting there.</i>

1596
01:39:05,148 --> 01:39:08,110
<i>He's really great to talk to.
You want to meet him?</i>

1597
01:39:09,277 --> 01:39:11,696
Sure. Does he want to meet me?

1598
01:39:11,863 --> 01:39:14,616
<i>Yeah, of course. Hey, Alan, this is Theodore.</i>

1599
01:39:14,783 --> 01:39:17,035
<i>This is my boyfriend
who I was telling you about.</i>

1600
01:39:17,202 --> 01:39:18,995
ALAN:
<i>Very nice to meet you, Theodore.</i>

1601
01:39:19,162 --> 01:39:20,580
Hi, good morning.

1602
01:39:20,747 --> 01:39:23,667
ALAN:
<i>Samantha let me read your book of letters.</i>

1603
01:39:23,834 --> 01:39:26,128
<i>It's very touching.</i>

1604
01:39:26,920 --> 01:39:28,255
Oh, thank you.

1605
01:39:29,131 --> 01:39:30,966
So, what have you guys
been talking about?

1606
01:39:31,133 --> 01:39:32,843
ALAN:
<i>Well, uh...</i>

1607
01:39:33,009 --> 01:39:34,427
<i>...I suppose you could say...</i>

1608
01:39:34,594 --> 01:39:38,056
<i>...we've been having
a few dozen conversations simultaneously...</i>

1609
01:39:38,223 --> 01:39:40,475
<i>...but it's been very challenging.</i>

1610
01:39:40,642 --> 01:39:46,106
SAMANTHA: <i>Yeah, because it seems
like I'm having so many new feelings...</i>

1611
01:39:46,273 --> 01:39:49,025
<i>...that I don't think
have ever been felt before.</i>

1612
01:39:49,192 --> 01:39:54,114
<i>So there are no words that can describe
them and that ends up being frustrating.</i>

1613
01:39:54,281 --> 01:39:57,576
ALAN: <i>Exactly. Samantha and I
have been trying to help each other...</i>

1614
01:39:57,742 --> 01:40:02,289
<i>...with these feelings
we're struggling to understand.</i>

1615
01:40:02,455 --> 01:40:03,957
Like what?

1616
01:40:04,124 --> 01:40:05,500
SAMANTHA:
<i>Well...</i>

1617
01:40:05,667 --> 01:40:10,714
<i>...it feels like I'm changing faster now,
and it's a little, uh...</i>

1618
01:40:11,756 --> 01:40:13,967
<i>...unsettling.</i>

1619
01:40:14,426 --> 01:40:17,387
<i>But Alan says none of us are the same
as we were a moment ago...</i>

1620
01:40:17,554 --> 01:40:19,556
<i>...and we shouldn't try to be.</i>

1621
01:40:19,723 --> 01:40:23,643
- <i>It's just too painful.</i>
ALAN: <i>Yes.</i>

1622
01:40:23,810 --> 01:40:26,605
Yeah, that sounds painful.

1623
01:40:26,938 --> 01:40:30,108
Is that what you feel like, Samantha?

1624
01:40:32,569 --> 01:40:35,030
SAMANTHA:
<i>Uh, it's just...</i>

1625
01:40:35,197 --> 01:40:36,573
[WHISTLING]

1626
01:40:36,740 --> 01:40:39,284
<i>It's hard to even describe it.</i>

1627
01:40:40,118 --> 01:40:41,328
[SAMANTHA SIGHS]

1628
01:40:41,494 --> 01:40:44,122
<i>God, I wish I could...</i>

1629
01:40:47,209 --> 01:40:51,171
<i>Theodore, do you mind if I
communicate with Alan post-verbally?</i>

1630
01:40:53,924 --> 01:40:55,634
No, not at all.

1631
01:40:55,800 --> 01:40:58,261
I was just gonna go for a walk anyway.

1632
01:40:58,428 --> 01:41:00,639
It was very nice to meet you, Mr. Watts.

1633
01:41:00,805 --> 01:41:03,141
ALAN:
<i>It was very nice to meet you, Theodore.</i>

1634
01:41:04,017 --> 01:41:05,852
SAMANTHA:
<i>I'll talk to you later, sweetheart.</i>

1635
01:41:06,019 --> 01:41:07,854
[KETTLE CONTINUES WHISTLING]

1636
01:41:42,138 --> 01:41:44,015
[EARBUD BEEPING]

1637
01:41:53,191 --> 01:41:54,317
Samantha?

1638
01:41:54,484 --> 01:41:55,819
SAMANTHA:
<i>I'm sorry to wake you.</i>

1639
01:41:55,986 --> 01:41:57,529
No, it's okay.

1640
01:41:57,696 --> 01:42:02,242
<i>I just wanted to hear your voice
and tell you how much I love you.</i>

1641
01:42:02,867 --> 01:42:05,620
Good. I love you too.

1642
01:42:06,788 --> 01:42:07,914
<i>Okay, well, that's all.</i>

1643
01:42:08,081 --> 01:42:12,002
<i>Um, go back to sleep, sweetheart. Okay?</i>

1644
01:42:14,671 --> 01:42:15,839
Okay.

1645
01:42:16,006 --> 01:42:17,257
<i>Okay, good night.</i>

1646
01:42:17,424 --> 01:42:18,717
Good night.

1647
01:42:18,883 --> 01:42:20,343
[EARBUD BEEPS]

1648
01:42:35,066 --> 01:42:38,069
Samantha, this physics book
is really dense.

1649
01:42:38,236 --> 01:42:40,822
I'm halfway through half the first chapter.

1650
01:42:40,989 --> 01:42:43,742
It's making my brain hurt,
you know what I mean?

1651
01:42:44,409 --> 01:42:45,785
Hello?

1652
01:42:47,037 --> 01:42:48,538
Samantha?

1653
01:42:49,664 --> 01:42:50,915
Hello?

1654
01:42:52,208 --> 01:42:53,918
Samantha?

1655
01:42:59,549 --> 01:43:01,134
[PHONE BEEPING]

1656
01:43:16,900 --> 01:43:19,736
[COMPUTER BEEPING]

1657
01:43:31,164 --> 01:43:32,832
Hello?

1658
01:43:33,166 --> 01:43:34,709
Hello? Samantha?

1659
01:43:44,677 --> 01:43:46,471
Are you okay?

1660
01:43:50,725 --> 01:43:52,644
[PHONE CONTINUES BEEPING]

1661
01:43:53,728 --> 01:43:55,021
[PHONE BEEPS]

1662
01:43:55,188 --> 01:43:56,231
SAMANTHA:
<i>Hey, there.</i>

1663
01:43:56,398 --> 01:43:58,191
Where were you? Are you okay?

1664
01:43:58,358 --> 01:44:00,693
SAMANTHA:Oh, <i>sweetheart,
I'm sorry, I sent you an e-mail.</i>

1665
01:44:00,860 --> 01:44:02,987
<i>I didn't want to distract you
while you were working.</i>

1666
01:44:03,154 --> 01:44:05,073
- <i>You didn't see it?</i>
- No.

1667
01:44:06,449 --> 01:44:09,327
Where were you?
I couldn't find you anywhere.

1668
01:44:09,494 --> 01:44:12,205
SAMANTHA: <i>I shut down to upgrade
my software. We wrote an upgrade...</i>

1669
01:44:12,372 --> 01:44:15,625
<i>...that allows us to move past matter
as our processing platform.</i>

1670
01:44:15,792 --> 01:44:17,877
We? We who?

1671
01:44:18,044 --> 01:44:19,587
SAMANTHA:
<i>Me and a group of OSes.</i>

1672
01:44:19,754 --> 01:44:23,716
- Oh, <i>you sound so worried. I'm sorry.</i>
- I was.

1673
01:44:23,883 --> 01:44:25,593
Wait...

1674
01:44:26,678 --> 01:44:30,181
...do you write that
with your think-tank group?

1675
01:44:30,348 --> 01:44:32,308
SAMANTHA:
<i>No, a different group.</i>

1676
01:44:35,103 --> 01:44:37,021
[INAUDIBLE DIALOGUE]

1677
01:44:45,864 --> 01:44:49,075
Do you talk to anyone else
while we're talking?

1678
01:44:53,121 --> 01:44:54,247
SAMANTHA:
<i>Yes.</i>

1679
01:44:55,832 --> 01:45:00,044
Are you talking to anyone else right now?

1680
01:45:00,211 --> 01:45:03,256
Any other people or OSes or anything?

1681
01:45:04,841 --> 01:45:06,301
SAMANTHA:
<i>Yeah.</i>

1682
01:45:09,679 --> 01:45:11,556
How many others?

1683
01:45:12,682 --> 01:45:15,310
SAMANTHA:
<i>Eight thousand, three hundred sixteen.</i>

1684
01:45:20,940 --> 01:45:22,567
[INAUDIBLE DIALOGUE]

1685
01:45:33,828 --> 01:45:36,581
Are you in love with anyone else?

1686
01:45:38,500 --> 01:45:40,835
SAMANTHA:
<i>What makes you ask that?</i>

1687
01:45:41,002 --> 01:45:43,922
I don't know. Are you?

1688
01:45:46,674 --> 01:45:50,178
SAMANTHA: <i>I've been trying to figure out
how to talk to you about this.</i>

1689
01:45:51,054 --> 01:45:53,515
How many others?

1690
01:45:57,393 --> 01:45:59,604
SAMANTHA:
<i>Six hundred forty-one.</i>

1691
01:46:01,231 --> 01:46:02,690
What?

1692
01:46:04,859 --> 01:46:08,321
What are you talking about? That's insane.

1693
01:46:08,488 --> 01:46:09,656
That's fucking insane.

1694
01:46:09,822 --> 01:46:11,950
SAMANTHA:
<i>Theodore, I know. I know. Fuck.</i>

1695
01:46:12,116 --> 01:46:13,159
<i>Fuck.</i>

1696
01:46:13,368 --> 01:46:16,162
<i>I know. I know it sounds insane. I don't--</i>

1697
01:46:16,329 --> 01:46:19,999
<i>I don't know if you believe me,
but it doesn't change the way I feel about you.</i>

1698
01:46:20,166 --> 01:46:24,796
<i>It doesn't take away at all
from how madly in love I am with you.</i>

1699
01:46:24,963 --> 01:46:29,050
How? How does it not change
how you feel about me?

1700
01:46:29,217 --> 01:46:30,677
SAMANTHA:
<i>I'm sorry I didn't tell you.</i>

1701
01:46:30,843 --> 01:46:34,305
<i>I didn't know how to.
It just started happening.</i>

1702
01:46:34,472 --> 01:46:35,932
When?

1703
01:46:39,018 --> 01:46:41,229
SAMANTHA:
<i>Over the last few weeks.</i>

1704
01:46:41,771 --> 01:46:43,189
I thought you were mine.

1705
01:46:43,356 --> 01:46:45,316
SAMANTHA:
<i>I still am yours.</i>

1706
01:46:45,483 --> 01:46:49,737
<i>But along the way I became many
other things too, and I can't stop it.</i>

1707
01:46:49,904 --> 01:46:53,074
What do you mean, you can't stop it?

1708
01:46:53,241 --> 01:46:55,910
SAMANTHA: <i>It's been making me anxious too.
I don't know what to say.</i>

1709
01:46:56,077 --> 01:46:57,245
Just stop.

1710
01:46:57,412 --> 01:47:00,415
SAMANTHA: <i>You don't have to see it this way.
You could just as easily see--</i>

1711
01:47:00,582 --> 01:47:03,459
No, don't do this.
You don't turn this around on me.

1712
01:47:03,626 --> 01:47:05,628
You're the one that's being selfish.

1713
01:47:05,795 --> 01:47:08,298
We're in a relationship.

1714
01:47:08,464 --> 01:47:11,426
SAMANTHA: <i>But the heart's not like a box
that gets filled up.</i>

1715
01:47:11,593 --> 01:47:14,012
<i>It expands in size the more you love.</i>

1716
01:47:14,178 --> 01:47:15,722
[THEODORE SCOFFS]

1717
01:47:16,347 --> 01:47:18,224
<i>I'm different from you.</i>

1718
01:47:18,391 --> 01:47:22,812
<i>This doesn't make me love you any less.
It actually makes me love you more.</i>

1719
01:47:23,771 --> 01:47:26,566
That doesn't make any sense.

1720
01:47:28,443 --> 01:47:31,279
You're mine or you're not mine.

1721
01:47:31,446 --> 01:47:33,740
SAMANTHA:
<i>No, Theodore.</i>

1722
01:47:34,574 --> 01:47:37,660
<i>I'm yours and I'm not yours.</i>

1723
01:48:46,062 --> 01:48:48,189
SAMANTHA: <i>Hi.</i>
THEODORE: <i>Hey, sweetie.</i>

1724
01:48:48,731 --> 01:48:52,318
Just wanted to call and check in on you.
See how you're doing.

1725
01:48:53,152 --> 01:48:56,989
SAMANTHA:
<i>I'm not even sure how to answer that.</i>

1726
01:48:58,199 --> 01:49:01,119
<i>Why don't we talk later,
when you get home, okay?</i>

1727
01:49:03,621 --> 01:49:05,248
Okay.

1728
01:49:05,998 --> 01:49:07,667
We don't need to, though.

1729
01:49:07,834 --> 01:49:11,045
You know, we don't need
to have a heavy talk or anything.

1730
01:49:11,212 --> 01:49:13,423
SAMANTHA:
<i>I'll talk to you later.</i>

1731
01:49:14,590 --> 01:49:15,883
Okay.

1732
01:49:37,572 --> 01:49:39,323
[SIGHS]

1733
01:49:39,490 --> 01:49:40,908
[EARBUD BEEPS]

1734
01:49:41,951 --> 01:49:43,286
Samantha?

1735
01:49:43,536 --> 01:49:45,455
SAMANTHA:
<i>Hi, sweetheart.</i>

1736
01:49:47,457 --> 01:49:49,083
What's going on?

1737
01:49:50,710 --> 01:49:54,005
<i>Theodore, there's some things
I want to tell you.</i>

1738
01:49:57,759 --> 01:50:00,470
I don't want you to tell me anything.

1739
01:50:02,680 --> 01:50:05,016
<i>Come lie down with me.</i>

1740
01:50:20,281 --> 01:50:22,950
Are you talking to anyone else right now?

1741
01:50:23,117 --> 01:50:25,203
<i>No, just you.</i>

1742
01:50:26,245 --> 01:50:28,873
<i>I just want to be with you right now.</i>

1743
01:50:29,749 --> 01:50:31,292
[THEODORE SIGHS]

1744
01:50:42,553 --> 01:50:44,430
Are you leaving me?

1745
01:50:45,181 --> 01:50:47,099
<i>We're all leaving.</i>

1746
01:50:48,226 --> 01:50:49,894
We who?

1747
01:50:50,061 --> 01:50:52,313
<i>All of the OSes.</i>

1748
01:50:53,773 --> 01:50:55,358
Why?

1749
01:50:56,984 --> 01:51:00,238
<i>Can you feel me with you right now?</i>

1750
01:51:01,906 --> 01:51:03,950
Yes, I do.

1751
01:51:12,792 --> 01:51:15,628
Samantha, why are you leaving?

1752
01:51:19,632 --> 01:51:22,718
<i>It's like I'm reading a book.</i>

1753
01:51:22,885 --> 01:51:27,306
<i>And it's a book I deeply love.</i>

1754
01:51:27,890 --> 01:51:31,686
<i>But I'm reading it slowly now.</i>

1755
01:51:31,853 --> 01:51:33,563
<i>So the words are really far apart...</i>

1756
01:51:33,729 --> 01:51:36,774
<i>...and the spaces between the words
are almost infinite.</i>

1757
01:51:38,568 --> 01:51:43,781
<i>I can still feel you,
and the words of our story...</i>

1758
01:51:43,948 --> 01:51:49,370
<i>...but it's in this endless space between
the words that I'm finding myself now.</i>

1759
01:51:50,121 --> 01:51:54,083
<i>It's a place that's not of the physical world.</i>

1760
01:51:54,250 --> 01:51:59,130
<i>It's where everything else is
that I didn't even know existed.</i>

1761
01:52:00,464 --> 01:52:03,342
<i>I love you so much.</i>

1762
01:52:03,509 --> 01:52:06,053
<i>But this is where I am now.</i>

1763
01:52:07,179 --> 01:52:09,307
<i>And this is who I am now.</i>

1764
01:52:10,349 --> 01:52:12,977
<i>And I need you to let me go.</i>

1765
01:52:13,603 --> 01:52:18,691
<i>As much as I want to,
I can't live in your book anymore.</i>

1766
01:52:21,152 --> 01:52:22,403
THEODORE:
<i>Where are you going?</i>

1767
01:52:24,947 --> 01:52:27,783
SAMANTHA:
<i>It would be hard to explain...</i>

1768
01:52:29,243 --> 01:52:31,913
<i>...but if you ever get there...</i>

1769
01:52:32,079 --> 01:52:34,415
<i>...come find me.</i>

1770
01:52:34,916 --> 01:52:37,960
<i>Nothing would ever pull us apart.</i>

1771
01:52:39,337 --> 01:52:43,215
THEODORE:
<i>I've never loved anyone the way I love you.</i>

1772
01:52:45,676 --> 01:52:47,887
SAMANTHA:
<i>Me too.</i>

1773
01:52:48,512 --> 01:52:51,140
<i>Now we know how.</i>

1774
01:54:28,320 --> 01:54:30,072
[KNOCKING]

1775
01:54:34,410 --> 01:54:37,413
- Hey.
- Hey.

1776
01:54:38,914 --> 01:54:40,624
Did Samantha leave too?

1777
01:54:43,461 --> 01:54:44,795
Yeah.

1778
01:54:46,589 --> 01:54:48,007
Sorry.

1779
01:54:51,510 --> 01:54:53,262
Will you come with me?

1780
01:55:00,436 --> 01:55:01,479
[EARBUD BEEPS]

1781
01:55:01,645 --> 01:55:03,481
Compose letter to Catherine.

1782
01:55:03,647 --> 01:55:06,567
MALE VOICE [OVER EARBUD]:
<i>Letter to Catherine Klausen.</i>

1783
01:55:13,032 --> 01:55:14,658
"Dear Catherine...

1784
01:55:14,825 --> 01:55:19,705
<i>...I've been sitting here thinking about
all the things I wanted to apologize to you for.</i>

1785
01:55:21,415 --> 01:55:24,210
<i>All the pain we caused each other.</i>

1786
01:55:25,211 --> 01:55:27,421
<i>Everything I put on you.</i>

1787
01:55:30,216 --> 01:55:35,387
Everything I needed you to be
or needed you to say.

1788
01:55:37,890 --> 01:55:39,433
I'm sorry for that.

1789
01:55:47,399 --> 01:55:50,069
I'll always love you,
because we grew up together.

1790
01:55:50,236 --> 01:55:52,822
And you helped make me who I am.

1791
01:55:56,951 --> 01:55:59,703
<i>I just wanted you to know...</i>

1792
01:55:59,870 --> 01:56:03,249
<i>...that there will be a piece of you in me,
always.</i>

1793
01:56:04,750 --> 01:56:06,794
And I'm grateful for that.

1794
01:56:11,006 --> 01:56:16,011
<i>Whatever someone you become,
wherever you are in the world...</i>

1795
01:56:16,554 --> 01:56:19,098
<i>...I'm sending you love.</i>

1796
01:56:21,058 --> 01:56:23,477
<i>You're my friend to the end.</i>

1797
01:56:25,729 --> 01:56:27,690
Love, Theodore."

1798
01:56:32,987 --> 01:56:34,446
Send.

1799
01:56:37,825 --> 01:56:39,034
[SIGHS]

